Ok, so Eklavya-B finally did it. We definitely have a wimpiest-ascension
contender here: level 25, 185/237 HP, -14 AC, stats 25,17,16,11,18,7,
a little short of 5M points. Anyone?

Other stats: killed Baalzebub, Asmodeus, Juiblex, Orcus, the WY 12
times (is this on the low side? recently saw a post with 26 WY scalps),
24 Archons (this is rather good isn't it, for such a weakling?)

As for me, this was my 3rd quest (the other two were Valkyries), second
trip to Gehennom, first visit to the sanctum and the elemental planes.

Wishes, and a steady stream of genocide scrolls (I used at least 6 I
believe) were the key to this one. First wishes were Mjollnir, Yendex and
GDSM, first genocides were master liches (un-IDed scroll, so no chance
to bless), Vs and ;s. Got my AC down to -19 from a lawful priest, then
converted the altar. He proved pretty tough (those kicks) so I had to
dig down. Went all the way down to the castle with no means of
levitation (I hate doing large bodies of water without levitation, being
careless with keystrokes) so came back up. Luckily, a cockatrice corpse
became available just as I approached the angry priest's level again, so
stoned him and took my gold back. (Later I prayed in Gehennom, and
Moloch took those 5 AC away from me again, but that's another story.)

Then I ate a nymph, used up another wish on a blessed RTC and went on
the quest. Easy, just level tport up and come down on the Thoth Amon as
he waits at the foot of the stairs. And whaddya know? the quest item
lets you levitate. Back to the castle. On the way down, Eklavya became
the Envoy of Balance and got Vorpal Blade. Having mainly played Vs,
I used to think Mjollnir was the ultimate weapon, but VB is really cool!

With the castle WW, I got a much-needed blessed ring of conflict, and
then tried a figurine of an Archon, for the first time. Sure enough I
lost him (and his Demonbane and SR) but he didn't turn wild on me. I
often saw him wandering aimlessly and peacefully round on the Medusa
level. (I later got Eklavya a figurine of a lurker above, they make
cool pets, if you remember to take off your RC when they come near
you. Angels, minotaurs, whatever: Burrrp!)

With conflict, and having eaten a black dragon to get my final
intrinsic, genocided Ds (saves time) and wished for a shield of
reflection. The maze levels were pretty dull. I was planning to let
peaceful Orcus alone, except Eklavya spied him using a wand of death on
a minotaur, so he whacked him and took his wand away. I wouldn't have
known how to get into the sanctum without rec.games.hack, but with
outside help it was easy. Orcus's wand got the high priest, but the
first time I entered the temple it was uncharged and the high priest
sure surprised me with the fury of his attack. That used up Vlad's ALS.
Later I took all the useless amulets and made myeslf several ALSs, I
guess the purists wouldn't like that. But then you wouldn't like my
Yendex card either: I like it, it allows me to play a wandmaster
character instead of just whackwhackwhack. Those 24 Archon scalps that
Eklavya collected were mostly wand work: slow monster and cancellation,
then a few strokes with VB usually takes his head off.

Went into the endgame with no means of removing curse, no potions, no
scrolls, and much trepidation. It could have been pretty boring hunting
for the portals, luckily (and this I think was real *luck* not NH luck)
none of them took too much time. When I had too many cursed items, I
prayed to Crom, and instead of handing me some useless object, as he
often did, the silly bugger, he actually made it all glow amber. On the
astral plane, Death did his draining life bit, and had me worried, but
I had my RC on, and this purple worm came along and... Burrrp!

Crom's altar was, of course, in the third temple I visited. Never
encountered Pestilence or Famine, though they were there in all their
magenta glory.

Piece of cake. (I did say it was a boast!)

Reading rgh over the last some months, I gather that ascension carries
with it the privilege of making gratuitous comments about the game
directed to the dev.team. Here goes:

If you ask me what the most useful item in this game is: I'd now have to
say ring of conflict. But different things are useful at different
times, and I have no complaints about game balance.

Too many maze levels, but the main irritation was that Eklavya came
across so few mapping scrolls, and couldn't write the spellbook. (No
rocket scientist he, see stats above.) I guess with mapping and t&tc
they aren't too bad.

I couldn't figure out what those blank areas in the water plane were
supposed to be, and why they made you lurch around drunkenly. Terribly
annoying, especially since there are no landmarks, and you are trying
to scour every square to find the portal.

The Yendex card allows you to play mainly with wands, and I really like
that. I'd hate to see that privilege taken away from my neutral non-Ts.

Polymorphing objects is built into the game, and I don't see why it's
considered abuse. At least, I don't see why people speak of it in the
same breath as backing up save files. Similarly the "cursed bell trick"
about which I've recently been enlightened. (As you can see, I didn't
use it.) Any sequence of 1s and 0s you send the program to take it to
the desired conclusion is legitimate, and is not the same as stepping
outside and mucking around with the files the program creates.

I'd like to see the wizard mode's ^O feature implemented for normal
play, modified of course to map you only the levels you've visited.
Should be simple enough to do, no?

Cheers,
